  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multi-profile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc, only marginally above RNA-only avgpool (0.591). The image-only model was very weak (0.208), raising uncertainty about whether the image features are contributing at all or being diluted. The fusion mechanism is the one design axis not yet varied in the multimodal setting. Question: Does weighted fusion (config_019) outperform concat, indicating that modality-level scaling/balancing is important given the large gap in per-modality signal strength? Why best next step: It is a single-variable ablation of the current best config, directly testing whether the simple concatenation is optimal or whether explicit weighting can better leverage the (apparently weaker) image branch. This is low-risk, high-information: a positive result opens the weighted-fusion family across encoders/profiles, while a null result confirms concat suffices and redirects budget toward stronger image encoders or RNA encoders."
